  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between N-Formylmethionine and Cytochrome c oxidase subunit 7C, mitochondrial, through a series of target interactions involving cholic acid. N-Formylmethionine is identified as a target of multiple cytochrome c oxidase subunit isoforms, specifically subunit 2, 7B, and 5A, all of which are targets of cholic acid. Cholic acid, in turn, is linked to the subunit 7C, mitochondrial, indicating a possible pathway where N-Formylmethionine may influence the activity or expression of these subunits through cholic acid. The consistent scores across the three paths (final_score=0.745) suggest a strong, albeit indirect, relationship, likely mediated by cholic acid as a common intermediary. The evidence supports a mechanistic link where N-Formylmethionine may act through cholic acid to modulate the function of cytochrome c oxidase subunit 7C, mitochondrial. However, the exact nature of this interaction remains uncertain, and further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the direct involvement of N-Formylmethionine in this process.",
